// A box, of the prelude. `own value` moves a value to the heap, and
// `unbox(boxed)` takes it back: what a recursive type holds boxed, wanted
// again as a value among others.

/// The value a box holds, taken out of it, and the box freed. Nothing is
/// dropped, since the value lives on in what this answers; the box is
/// moved by the call, so using it afterwards is a use after a move.
@intrinsic
pub fn unbox<T>(boxed: own<T>): T
